1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,372
Twelve

2
00:00:03,372 --> 00:00:33,992
On March 26 the Israeli military said Revolutionary Guards navy commander Alireza Tangsiri had been killed in an airstrike in Bandar Abbas, and the Revolutionary Guards confirmed it. He had led the navy since 2018 and directed the blockade of Hormuz. The same day two teenagers were killed in strikes on homes in Shiraz, and in Abu Dhabi two civilians were killed by debris from an intercepted Iranian missile. The gatekeeper of the strait had been erased.

3
00:00:34,592 --> 00:01:04,660
Colonel Darius Sepahvand had not slept at all. In the morning there was a one-line text from a number he did not know. Baba, I’m okay. Where she was, who she was with, whether she had water. Nothing. He read the line a hundred times. After a hundred times it was still one line. At noon an order came down. Recruitment from the age of twelve. He put it on the desk. It was not his hand that was shaking. It was the paper.

4
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:32,568
When Narges was twelve, she would try on her father’s uniform cap before she got out of the car. The cap was big. It came down over her eyes. She laughed. What he had spent thirty-one years trying to protect was not a country that put that cap on a child and stood her at a checkpoint. On March 11 an eleven-year-old boy had died at a Tehran checkpoint, and Amnesty International called the mobilization of children a war crime.

5
00:01:33,168 --> 00:02:02,012
In 1987 his older brother died on the southern front, a seventeen-year-old volunteer. He went with a plastic key around his neck. The key to paradise, they said. Thirteen-year-old Darius watched their mother get the key back and put it in a drawer. Eight years later he put on the uniform his brother should have worn, swearing no seventeen-year-old would ever die like that again. His brother was not the only boy with a key like that.

6
00:02:02,612 --> 00:02:30,808
For thirty-one years he had never taken out that vow. Today he did. The vow had died long ago. Darius made his decision. He had a head that knew this command post’s network, and the memory of a cable: the coordinates of the Fordow air-defense zone, and three lines on what was spinning under that mountain. The country he had meant to protect was outside it. Getting out takes longer than getting in. First you have to find the door.

7
00:02:31,408 --> 00:02:35,220
Epic Fury continues in Episode 11.
